t3_thread_send calls: before=0 after=1

=== 3. the failed run's recovery resumes the still-counted generation (positive control) ===
probe=relaunchable resume=1
relaunched=yes
t3_thread_send calls: before=1 after=2

=== 4. reconciliation reclaims the failed generation (dead-after-start) ===
fleet-seats: reclaimed id=t3mate generation=g-fail (dead-after-start)
reclaim rc=0
seat lifecycle: reclaimed

=== 5. recovery must not resume the reclaimed generation ===
probe=skipped|the T3 incarnation is terminal; normal capacity admission is required before resuming
relaunched=no
t3_thread_send calls: before=2 after=2

=== 6. the shared T3 turn-start boundary refuses the reclaimed generation ===
send_text_submit rc=0 out=error: T3 turn refused for t3mate; normal capacity admission is required send-failed
t3_thread_send calls: before=2 after=2
resume_failed rc=1 out=error: T3 turn refused for t3mate; normal capacity admission is required
t3_thread_send calls: before=2 after=2

=== 7. removing the task record does not unlock the reclaimed thread ===
no-meta send rc=0 out=error: T3 turn refused for t3mate; normal capacity admission is required send-failed
t3_thread_send calls: before=2 after=2

=== 8. another local caller state cannot bypass the reclaimed thread ===
other-home send rc=0 out=error: T3 turn refused for t3mate; normal capacity admission is required send-failed
t3_thread_send calls: before=2 after=2

=== 9. capacity is genuinely free for a replacement seat ===
fleet-seats: reserved pool=t3pool id=contender generation=g-other used=1 capacity=1
reserve contender rc=0
